  patientNotes: 'Patient: Mang Ben (58 years old)

    Companion: Aling Nelia (wife),
    55 years old

    Setting: Emergency Room, Tertiary Hospital, Philippines

    Reason
    for Visit: Jaw and back pain, cannot open mouth (lockjaw)

    Notes from Nurse:
    Patient is a farmer. Stepped on a rusty nail 10 days ago while working in the
    field. Did not receive tetanus vaccine. Now presenting with trismus (lockjaw),
    muscle rigidity, and difficulty swallowing. Spasms triggered by minor stimuli.
    Wife is terrified.



'
  interactPrompt: {fileID: 769436024}
