  patientNotes: 'Patient: Alex (7 years old, male)

    Companion: Marlie (mother),
    32 years old

    Setting: Primary Care Clinic / Rural Health Unit, Philippines

    Reason
    for Visit: High fever for 3 days, not going down, body pain, rash

    Notes
    from Nurse: Child looks flushed and lethargic. Mother reports fever has not subsided
    since it started. Child has infrequent bumps on the body. Has not been vomiting.
    No nosebleed or gum bleeding noted. Lives in a community with ongoing dengue
    cases. Mother is anxious.'
  interactPrompt: {fileID: 1048859825}
